meta {
  name: Get Producer Drawer
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/management-dashboard/producers/{{managementProducerId}}?range=ytd
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  range: ytd
  ~leadSourceIds: {{mailerLeadSourceId}}
  ~policyTypes: Auto
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{managementDashboardToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    // Run `Get Team` first — it captures the first row's producer id.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the header is the producer", function () {
    const { producer } = res.getBody();
    expect(producer.producerId).to.equal(bru.getVar("managementProducerId"));
    expect(producer.initials).to.be.a("string");
  });

  test("the stats strip carries the row's four figures", function () {
    const { stats } = res.getBody();
    expect(stats).to.have.all.keys(
      "householdsQuoted", "householdsSold", "householdCloseRatio", "openAuditItems",
    );
  });

  test("the pipeline is open leads, most recently worked first", function () {
    const leads = res.getBody().activePipeline;
    for (const lead of leads) {
      expect(["Sold", "Converted", "Not Qualified", "Lost", "Closed"]).to.not.include(lead.status);
      expect(lead.ageDays).to.be.at.least(0);
    }
    const stamps = leads.map((lead) => lead.lastActivityAt).filter(Boolean).map(Date.parse);
    for (let i = 1; i < stamps.length; i++) {
      expect(stamps[i - 1]).to.be.at.least(stamps[i]);
    }
  });

  test("the open items are the ones the column counts", function () {
    const { stats, openAuditItems } = res.getBody();
    // Equal unless the list hit its cap — 200 is far past any demo tenant.
    expect(openAuditItems.length).to.equal(stats.openAuditItems);
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /management-dashboard/producers/:producerId — the producer drawer (PAC-139)

  What a Team Activity row opens: the producer's header and availability, the
  **same four figures** as their row, their **Active Pipeline**, and their
  **open audit items** one row each.

  - **Module / permission / filter:** as `Get Alerts`. The person is the path
    parameter; the query's `producerIds` is ignored.
  - **Scope:** the producer must be in the caller's scope, else `404` — the
    same answer a wrong id gets, so the response never confirms a colleague
    exists in another branch.

  ## Active Pipeline
  The leads the producer is working on: created in the window, status not
  terminal, source and line-of-business filters applied, most recently worked
  first, capped at 50. The **stage is the lead's own Status field** ("go to your
  status field … those are your stat[us]" — David, 00:24:04).

  | field | notes |
  |---|---|
  | lineOfBusiness | what the lead asked to have quoted, joined with ` · `; `null` when intake recorded nothing (every migrated lead) |
  | ageDays | whole days since the lead was created |
  | value | the latest quote recap's premium, or `null` when none was written |

  ## Open audit items
  One row per failed, unresolved item on the producer's deals — all time, the
  set `stats.openAuditItems` counts — oldest first, capped at 200. Each opens
  the household until the Deal Audit page ships (PAC-106).

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "period": { "key": "ytd", "current": { "from": "2026-01-01", "to": "2026-09-23" }, "previous": { "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-09-23" } },
    "producer": { "producerId": "66f0…11", "name": "Pat Producer", "initials": "PP", "availability": "available" },
    "stats": { "householdsQuoted": 12, "householdsSold": 7, "householdCloseRatio": 58.3, "openAuditItems": 2 },
    "activePipeline": [
      { "leadId": "66f0…a1", "name": "Dana Whitfield", "householdId": "66f0…b2", "status": "Quoted",
        "lineOfBusiness": "Auto · Home", "ageDays": 9, "value": 2140, "lastActivityAt": "2026-09-22T16:40:00.000Z" }
    ],
    "openAuditItems": [
      { "dealAuditId": "66f0…c3", "dealId": "66f0…d4", "householdId": "66f0…b2", "clientName": "Dana Whitfield",
        "itemTitle": "Prior Insurance", "daysOpen": 12, "soldDate": "2026-09-11T05:00:00.000Z" }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  | status | when |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | `producerId` is not a record id, or a bad query (as `Get Alerts`) |
  | 404 | no such user in the agency, or one outside the caller's branch |
  | 401 / 403 | as `Get Alerts` |
}
